From f90ab65704f74ed4dfb9324de4bb99240bfc2b0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 09:11:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix quote PDF logo race, stale tagline, and dropped
 labour/delivery line items

- openPrintWindow: the 1.8s print fallback called doPrint() directly,
  bypassing the logo-load wait entirely. If the iframe's load event fired
  late (or not at all, e.g. because it happened synchronously during
  doc.close() before the listener was attached) and the fallback timer is
  what triggers printing, the logo image had no guarantee of being loaded
  yet. Now the fallback also waits for the logo before printing.

- printOrderQuote: whenever an order had a linked quoteId, this
  unconditionally reprinted the ORIGINAL quote's stored line items via
  printSavedQuote(), ignoring the order's own lineItems entirely. So
  Labour / Delivery Fee rows added later via "Edit Order" never showed up
  on the printed Quote (though they always worked correctly on the
  Invoice, which already read order.lineItems first). Order line items now
  take priority, falling back to the source quote's items only when the
  order has none of its own - matching printInvoice's existing behavior.

- loadContactDetails (app.js) fetched businessTagline from /api/settings
  but never applied it anywhere. The tagline shown on index.html,
  quote.html, products.html and gallery.html was a hardcoded literal
  ("You bring it. We brand it.") that Settings had no way to affect. Added
  a data-contact-tagline hook to all four pages and wired it up the same
  way as the existing email/location hooks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BQ6TyPJYWyobqGBSY1neoM
